    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d688">

                <pb facs="0646" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5833</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Curtis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-13T09:00:00-00:43">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1917, 9 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.42 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday Liberian Government received the following cablegram: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>British and French Governments advise declaration of war. Will guarantee
                            protection. Trade restrictions will be removed. Crommelin.<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d688-f1"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Liberian Government awaits the advice of the Government of the United States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Curtis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d688-f1" n="2" xml:id="d688-f1-content">
                <p>Liberian Minister in Great Britain.</p>
